 @page documentation_toolchains_llvm Native LLVM

<div style="background-color: #cfc ; padding: 10px; border: 1px solid green;"> 
You will find examples how this toolchain is used on particular machines on the page @ref page_machines.
</div>

### General Compiler Flag Remarks

Should you use ```-ffast-math``` this leads to inaccuracies in some applications,
such as ccz4. If this flag is desired, also use ```-frounding-math``` to avoid rounding
errors.
Clang enables fused multiply add operations via ```-ffp-contract=on``` instead of ```-fma```.


### OpenMP

For NVIDIA GPUs:

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
export MARCH=sm_XX
CC=clang CXX=clang++ ./configure --with-multithreading=omp --with-gpu=omp CXXFLAGS="-std=c++17 -O3 -W -Wall -Wno-attributes -fopenmp -fopenmp-targets=nvptx64-nvidia-cuda -Xopenmp-target=nvptx64-nvidia-cuda -march=$MARCH" LDFLAGS="-march=native -mtune=native -fopenmp -fopenmp-targets=nvptx64-nvidia-cuda -Xopenmp-target=nvptx64-nvidia-cuda -march=$MARCH"
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

where XX has to be replaced by the actual compute capability of the device.

Note: We set the C++ compiler standard to 17. This is due to an issue with LLVM Clang itself. See https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/61327.

### Using MLIR

Building a benchmark that uses MLIR requires our dslhype-opt executable, which must first be built.
Navigate to src/exahype2/mlir and enter the commands
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
mkdir build && cd build
cmake ..
cmake --build .
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
The output bin directory should then be added to your PATH.

When using GPU offloading with MLIR we require that the GPU vendor and architecture is set more explicitly when configuring Peano.
This is done with --with-gpu-vendor=amd|nvidia and --with-gpu-architecture=gfxXXX|sm_XX.
With these options set you do not need to the relevant flags in CXXFLAGS and LDFLAGS.

### Building MLIR

MLIR is not necessarily included in an LLVM install, so it may be necessary to build from source.
First, clone llvm from GitHub.

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project.git
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

In general, building MLIR just involves adding "mlir" to the LLVM_ENABLE_PROJECTS CMake option.
See https://mlir.llvm.org/getting_started/ for information. However, we generally want to build with
offloading support. To do so follow the following steps. Note that it assumes the existence of some clang version,
but we will build a new version of it.

It is simplest to build separately for AMD and NVIDIA offloading so that AMD libraries don't end up with
CUDA dependencies and vice-versa.

#### Setup for NVIDIA GPUS
The easiest way to build for offloading is to use the premade CMake cache file (llvm-project/offload/cmake/caches/Offload.cmake).
Some modifications are required though.
";mlir" should be added to LLVM_ENABLE_PROJECTS, "amdgcn-amd-amdhsa" should be removed from LLVM_RUNTIME_TARGETS,
and any lines that set AMD variables only should be removed. The resulting file should look something like
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
set(LLVM_ENABLE_PROJECTS "clang;clang-tools-extra;lld;mlir" CACHE STRING "")
set(LLVM_ENABLE_RUNTIMES "compiler-rt;libunwind;libcxx;libcxxabi;openmp;offload" CACHE STRING "")
set(LLVM_ENABLE_PER_TARGET_RUNTIME_DIR ON CACHE BOOL "")

set(LLVM_RUNTIME_TARGETS default;nvptx64-nvidia-cuda CACHE STRING "")
#set(RUNTIMES_nvptx64-nvidia-cuda_CACHE_FILES "${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/../libcxx/cmake/caches/NVPTX.cmake" CACHE STRING "")
#set(RUNTIMES_nvptx64-nvidia-cuda_LLVM_ENABLE_RUNTIMES "compiler-rt;libc;openmp;libcxx;libcxxabi" CACHE STRING "")
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

PATH, LIBRARY_PATH and LD_LIBRARY_PATH should be set to include CUDA. On COSMA this is
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
export PATH=/cosma/local/Nvidia-hpc-sdk/2025_253/Linux_x86_64/25.3/cuda/12.8/bin/:$PATH
export LIBRARY_PATH=/cosma/local/Nvidia-hpc-sdk/2025_253/Linux_x86_64/25.3/cuda/12.8/lib64:$LIBRARY_PATH
export LIBRARY_PATH=/cosma/local/Nvidia-hpc-sdk/2025_253/Linux_x86_64/25.3/cuda/12.8/compat/:$LIBRARY_PATH
export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/cosma/local/Nvidia-hpc-sdk/2025_253/Linux_x86_64/25.3/cuda/12.8/lib64:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
The version must be less than 13.0, which is not supported as of LLVM 22.1.8.

#### Setup for AMD GPUS
The easiest way to build for offloading is to use the premade CMake cache file (llvm-project/offload/cmake/caches/Offload.cmake).
Some modifications are required though.
";mlir" should be added to LLVM_ENABLE_PROJECTS, "nvptx64-nvidia-cuda" should be removed from LLVM_RUNTIME_TARGETS,
and any lines that set NVIDIA variables only should be removed. The resulting file should look something like
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
set(LLVM_ENABLE_PROJECTS "clang;clang-tools-extra;lld;mlir" CACHE STRING "")
set(LLVM_ENABLE_RUNTIMES "compiler-rt;libunwind;libcxx;libcxxabi;openmp;offload" CACHE STRING "")
set(LLVM_ENABLE_PER_TARGET_RUNTIME_DIR ON CACHE BOOL "")

set(LLVM_RUNTIME_TARGETS default;amdgcn-amd-amdhsa CACHE STRING "")
set(RUNTIMES_amdgcn-amd-amdhsa_CACHE_FILES "${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/../libcxx/cmake/caches/AMDGPU.cmake" CACHE STRING "")
set(RUNTIMES_amdgcn-amd-amdhsa_LLVM_ENABLE_RUNTIMES "compiler-rt;libc;openmp;libcxx;libcxxabi" CACHE STRING "")
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

PATH, LIBRARY_PATH and LD_LIBRARY_PATH should be set to include ROCm. On COSMA this is
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
export PATH=/cosma/local/rocm/7.2/bin/:$PATH
export LIBRARY_PATH=/cosma/local/rocm/7.2/lib/:$LIBRARY_PATH
export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/cosma/local/rocm/7.2/lib/:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

#### Building 
Finally run the following commands
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
cd llvm-project
mkdir build
CC=clang CXX=clang++ cmake -S llvm -B build -C $(pwd)/offload/cmake/caches/Offload.cmake \
      -DLLVM_TARGETS_TO_BUILD="host;NVPTX" \   # Replace NVPTX with AMDGPU to build for AMD GPUs
      -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
      -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=$(pwd)/../llvm-nvidia \ # Choose an appropriate name/location for the install location
      -G "Ninja" \
      -DLIBOMPTARGET_NVPTX_COMPUTE_CAPABILITIES="80,90" \ # Remove this line if building for AMD GPUs
      -DLIBOMP_ARCH="x86_64" \
      -DOMPTARGET_ENABLE_DEBUG=ON \
      -DLIBOMPTARGET_DLOPEN_PLUGINS=""
cd build
ninja
ninja install
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

To use the built compiler remember to set environment variables appropriately. Here we show
the settings when using an NVIDIA GPU, where ${LLVM_INSTALL_DIRECTORY} is llvm-project/install-x86.
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
export PATH=${LLVM_INSTALL_DIRECTORY}/bin/:$PATH
export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=${LLVM_INSTALL_DIRECTORY}/lib/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH
export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=${LLVM_INSTALL_DIRECTORY}/lib/amdgcn-amd-amdhsa:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

 */
 
